cff-version: "1.2.0"
type: software

title: "section-comment-outline: VS Code outline support for structured comment sections"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-06-06"

authors:
  - family-names: Case
    given-names: Denise M.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6165-7389"
    affiliation: "Northwest Missouri State University, School of Computer Science and Information Systems, Maryville, MO, USA"

repository-code: "https://github.com/denisecase/section-comment-outline"
url: "https://github.com/denisecase/section-comment-outline"
license: MIT

abstract: >
  section-comment-outline is a Visual Studio Code extension that exposes
  structured comment section headers as Outline symbols in repository,
  configuration, documentation, workflow, and metadata files. It supports
  navigation of files that do not otherwise provide useful document symbols,
  such as .gitattributes, CODEOWNERS, YAML workflows, TOML configuration,
  Markdown documents, and other operational project files.

keywords:
  - vscode
  - vscode-extension
  - outline
  - document-symbols
  - comments
  - navigation
  - developer-tools
  - typescript

message: "If using this work, please cite it as described in this file."
